description.narrative:
General question: Results related to the intended outcome 2015Question: Summarise results related to the intended outcome (this information will be sent to Open Aid)Answer: Summary of results 2014-2016: 

The project supported ten civil society organisations and networks with project grants and organisational development support grants to implement activities related to the above six objectives. The largest amount was provided for activities related to the 2015 elections. The partners’ projects contributed to the expected results and to the intended outcome: According to the external evaluation NPA has made good progress in achieving the outcome and expected results in all inter-related freedoms addressed by the project, i.e.: 
-The project Shalom has developed a Civic Education and Peace Education curriculum which it will continue to use for projects in conflict affected areas;
-Akhaya has been able to show that its model of empowering women through sexuality education works and is well accepted and are approached by many organisations asking Akghaya to provide training for them; 
-Paung Ku has mobilized communities in two locations to establish centers which bring together civil society actors to work on a common vision of human rights, diversity, inclusiveness, peace and environmental sustainability which will continue with funding from other donors. 

The external evaluation states further that the projects have been a good investment that will continue to be built upon by the local partners - also an indication of sustainability. All the projects have a strong element of raising civil society voice, either with national or local authorities or through the media.
